# Doom changes report

When work is on a Doom mod, or on another mod changed for the Doom install, track it through `00_Support/DoomLevelsSource/Doom-Changes-Report.md`. The `.txt` beside it is the copy to send. Keep the two in sync. Do not edit either file until the user accepts the proposed entry.

## Process

1. Start from an identified issue, or from updated files the user hands over.
2. Check those changes, or attempt the fix.
3. When the change is in the file, stop. Do not suggest a **Changes** entry yet. Wait until the user says they tested it and it worked. Then show one proposed **Changes** entry and ask whether to add it. Do not write the report in that same turn.
4. After an explicit yes, update **Changes**, **Files**, and **Players** in the `.md`, and the same words in the `.txt`. On `Doom-State.md`, set **Newest logged batch** to that date and title. If the entry closes an open issue, remove that issue from the state file and from **Known Issues**. Do not copy the entry body into the state file. In the `.md`, the Known Issues, Changes, Files, and Players headings use `#FF8A3D`. Dated headings and file-path headings use `#E2A0FF`. The `.txt` stays plain text. Section order is Known Issues, Changes, Files, Players.

A new tested change updates the three lists together:

- Add the entry at the top of **Changes**.
- Under **Files**, add one bullet per path: `mm/dd, hh:mm — Title` when the entry has a clock, or `mm/dd — Title` when it has a date only. Use the EDT date and time. No second time zone on the bullet. A new path gets a heading at the top of **Files**. An existing path gets the bullet at the top of that path, and that path moves to the top of **Files**.
- Add the title at the top of **Players**. Players is titles only.
- An entry with no path updates **Changes** and **Players** only.

When an existing **Changes** entry is updated, set its date and time to the current EDT and AWST time, move that entry to the top of **Changes**, update the matching **Files** bullet stamp and move that path to the top of **Files**, move that title to the top of **Players**, and set **Newest logged batch** to that date and title.

A fix that did not land, or that the user has not tested, does not get a **Changes** entry. Leave **Known Issues** as they are unless the user asks. A Known Issues heading is only `- Title`. No date and no time.

**Known Issues** is the first section. Read it when this work might already be listed there. Search **Changes**, **Files**, and **Players** for the mod folder or the topic. Do not read **Changes** from top to bottom. The entry shape below is enough to draft a proposal.

## Entry shape

A dated header is three lines. AWST is 12 hours ahead of EDT, and 13 hours ahead of EST. Use EDT when the US East Coast is on daylight time (UTC-4, roughly March–November) and EST when it is on standard time (UTC-5). AWST is UTC+8 all year. US date order is month/day/year. AWST date order is day/month/year. Time is 24-hour `hh:mm` plus am or pm.

The `.md` header has no parentheses. A colon follows the time zone. Both dates are month/day/year. The two time lines are one monospaced block so the dates and times share columns. Pad `EDT:` with two spaces and `AWST:` with one. Do not use a table. A `<br>` joins the title under them so the preview does not add a blank line:

```
EDT:  mm/dd/yyyy, hh:mm am
AWST: mm/dd/yyyy, hh:mm pm
- Title
```

The `.txt` header keeps parentheses, uses the same date order, and does not add am or pm. Same spacing, no table:

```
(EDT:  mm/dd/yyyy, hh:mm)
(AWST: mm/dd/yyyy, hh:mm)
- Title
```

Entries with no recorded clock time use the same aligned lines and the date only. Do not invent a clock time for them.

One change is one entry, even when it touches more than one mod. Title is a short result. The sentence says what changed and why, in the same plain style as the entries already in the report. Each path starts with the mod folder under `Mods`.

The date line stays at the left. Everything under it is indented four spaces.

```
### EDT:  10/04/2026, 01:46 am<br>AWST: 10/04/2026, 13:46 pm<br>- Slot Sizes for inventory and storages

    On 3.3 every inventory and storage slot is 64 instead of the new default of 73.

    - `zzz-FranticDansHUDbyAGF/Config/XUi_InGame/windows.xml`
```

Plain-text twin:

```
(EDT:  10/04/2026, 01:46)
(AWST: 10/04/2026, 13:46)
- Slot Sizes for inventory and storages
    On 3.3 every inventory and storage slot is 64 instead of the new default of 73.
    zzz-FranticDansHUDbyAGF/Config/XUi_InGame/windows.xml
```

## Files and Players

**Files** groups the paths from **Changes**. Newest path at the top. Newest bullet at the top of that path. The bullet uses the EDT stamp only.

```
### `ZZZ_DoomMod_Standalone/Config/items.xml`

    - 10/04, 21:57 — Mancubus fires two shots with a wider spread
    - 10/03 — Boiled water restores more and infects less
```

Plain-text twin:

```
ZZZ_DoomMod_Standalone/Config/items.xml
    - 10/04, 21:57 — Mancubus fires two shots with a wider spread
    - 10/03 — Boiled water restores more and infects less
```

**Players** is the **Changes** titles only, newest first.

```
- Mancubus fires two shots with a wider spread
- Boiled water restores more and infects less
```
